Few anime capture the late-90s golden era of sci-fi quite like *Martian Successor Nadesico* (<ruby>機動戦艦<rt>きどうせんかん</rt></ruby>ナデシコ). Premiering in October 1996, the series arrived right when the anime industry was still reeling from the psychological deconstruction of *Neon Genesis Evangelion*. Instead of sinking entirely into bleak despair, *Nadesico* struck a brilliant balance between high-stakes space opera, sharp parody, and heartfelt mecha nostalgia.

Episode 1 wastes zero time throwing its audience into the deep end, setting up Earth's desperate war against the "Jovian Lizards" and introducing Akito Tenkawa—a refugee who wants nothing to do with saving humanity if it interferes with his culinary dreams.

