A second iconic moment in Episode 1 features the bubbly yet tactically brilliant Captain Yurika Misumaru, greeting Akito in the middle of a warzone with zero gravity and zero situational awareness:

> 「アキトちゃん！やっと<ruby>会<rt>あ</rt></ruby>えたね！」  
> (*Akito-chan! Yatto aeta ne!*)

* **Literal Translation:** "Akito-chan! We finally were able to meet, right?"
* **Natural / Official Subtitle:** "Akito! I've been searching everywhere for you!"

#### Vocabulary & Grammar Breakdown

- **ちゃん** <span class="badge badge-particle">Particle</span>: Diminutive honorific suffix used for children, pets, or beloved childhood friends, signaling Yurika's persistent crush and utter refusal to treat Akito like an ordinary soldier.
- **やっと** <span class="badge badge-adj">Adj</span> / Adverb: "At long last / finally" — Highlights relief after a lengthy, arduous effort.
- **<ruby>会<rt>あ</rt></ruby>えた** <span class="badge badge-verb">Verb</span>: Potential past form of <ruby>会<rt>あ</rt></ruby>う (*au*, "to meet") — Signifies that overcoming the separation was an achievement.
- **ね** <span class="badge badge-particle">Particle</span>: Sentence-ending agreement marker ("isn't it?", "right?").

